[*] GTKWave save file for the Sparkle NoC wormhole router testbench.
[*] Loaded automatically by:  IP/NoC/wave/run.sh --view
[*]
[*] The story, top to bottom:
[*]   Stimulus  — two sources, both offering flits, neither backing off.
[*]   Injection — the flits ENTERING the router, decoded.  acceptA/acceptB
[*]               are the handshakes firing: acceptB pulses five times
[*]               while acceptA stays flat.  Both dest = (3,1), so XY
[*]               routing sends both to the SAME output.  That is the
[*]               collision the router has to resolve.
[*]   East port — the contended output: Head,Body,Body,Body,Tail  TWICE,
[*]               cleanly.  kind = 0/1/2 = Head/Body/Tail.  Payload tags
[*]               0xb0.. then 0xa0.. — two contiguous runs, no mixing.
[*]   Backpressure — inR0 held LOW for the five cycles B owns East, so
[*]               idxA freezes at 0.  The loser waits; it is not corrupted.
[*]
[dumpfile] "router.vcd"
[savefile] "router.gtkw"
